# libjxl -- the JPEG XL reference implementation, and the ONLY reason it is here
# is the gdk-pixbuf loader it ships.
#
# The GNOME 48 wallpapers are JPEG XL. gdk-pixbuf 2.42.12 ships no JXL loader
# and cannot be made to: the loader lives in THIS package, not in gdk-pixbuf,
# and this tree's gdk-pixbuf is built -Dothers=enabled, which covers only
# ani/bmp/gif/icns/ico/pnm/qtif/tga/xbm/xpm. Without this package
# gnome-backgrounds installs correctly, every image is verifiably present, CI is
# green, and the desktop shows no wallpaper. That gap was recorded as known when
# gnome-backgrounds was packaged; this closes it.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env. BLFS
# 12.4 carries 0.11.1.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/libjxl/libjxl/archive/v0.11.1/libjxl-0.11.1.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=1492dfef8dd6c3036446ac3b340005d92ab92f7d48ee3271b5dac1d36945d3d9
SRC_DIR=libjxl-0.11.1

# A GitHub archive URL ends in the bare tag.
SRC_FILE=libjxl-0.11.1.tar.gz

# EVERY third_party/ SUBMODULE DIRECTORY IN THIS TARBALL IS EMPTY.
#
# GitHub archives do not include submodule contents, so third_party/brotli,
# highway, lcms, libjpeg-turbo, libpng, skcms, sjpeg, googletest and zlib are
# all present as bare directories with nothing in them. That is not a defect --
# every one of those is a package this tree already has, or is about to -- but
# it decides how several options below have to be set, because the build file
# chooses bundled-or-system by testing whether those directories have contents.
#
# The two that fail LOUDLY if the system copy is missing, which is the good
# case: third_party/CMakeLists.txt:34-40 (highway, FATAL_ERROR naming
# find_package(HWY 1.0.7)) and :51-57 (brotli, FATAL_ERROR). lcms2 is the same
# shape at :108-112, gated on JPEGXL_ENABLE_SKCMS being off.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_PLUGINS=ON IS THE WHOLE POINT AND ITS DEFAULT IS **false**.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# CMakeLists.txt:147 reads `set(JPEGXL_ENABLE_PLUGINS false CACHE BOOL ...)`.
# Leave it alone and libjxl builds, installs, passes every assertion a naive
# recipe would write, and ships NO gdk-pixbuf loader -- which is the only file
# this package exists to provide.
#
# It gets worse one level down, and this is the trap worth reading twice.
# plugins/gdk-pixbuf/CMakeLists.txt:11-15 is:
#
#   if (NOT Gdk-Pixbuf_FOUND)
#     message(WARNING "GDK Pixbuf development libraries not found, \
#                      the Gdk-Pixbuf plugin will not be built")
#     return ()
#   endif ()
#
# A WARNING AND A RETURN, NOT AN ERROR. So even with plugins enabled, if
# gdk-pixbuf is not present at build time the loader is silently dropped and the
# build still succeeds. A warning inside a passing build reads as noise. That is
# why gdk-pixbuf is declared in [dependencies] and why install.sh ASSERTS the
# built loader rather than trusting this flag: the flag can be right and the
# outcome still wrong.
#
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_PLUGIN_GIMP210=OFF: defaults ON, and soft-skips exactly like
# the pixbuf plugin (plugins/gimp/CMakeLists.txt:9-12, warning + return) because
# GIMP is not packaged. Pinned off rather than left to that skip -- a soft-skip
# that happens to do what is wanted today is not a decision, and if GIMP is ever
# packaged this would start building a GIMP plugin nobody asked for.
#
# The MIME plugin is left ON, its default. It installs one file,
# share/mime/packages/image-jxl.xml, which is what makes a .jxl file identify as
# an image; the image build already runs update-mime-database. No path conflict:
# nothing else in this tree owns that filename.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Options forced off because the thing they need is not in the tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_SKCMS=OFF. THIS ONE DEFAULTS ON HERE. CMakeLists.txt:99-103
# computes the default from endianness -- NO on big-endian, YES otherwise -- and
# both architectures this tree builds for are little-endian, so the default is
# YES on x86_64 and aarch64 alike. skcms lives in third_party/skcms, which is
# empty. Turning it off is also what selects lcms2 as the colour engine, which
# is why lcms2 is a real dependency below rather than an optional extra.
#
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_SJPEG=OFF: defaults true (CMakeLists.txt:137);
# third_party/sjpeg is empty.
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_JPEGLI=OFF: CMakeLists.txt:90-95 already resolves this to NO
# by testing for third_party/libjpeg-turbo/jconfig.h.in and printing "libjpeg-
# turbo submodule is absent; not enabling jpegli". Pinned anyway, for the same
# reason as the GIMP plugin: that is a correct answer arrived at by accident.
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_JNI=OFF: defaults true; needs Java.
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_OPENEXR=OFF: defaults true; OpenEXR is not packaged.
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_MANPAGES=OFF: defaults true; needs asciidoc, not packaged.
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_DOXYGEN=OFF: defaults true; needs doxygen, not packaged.
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_BENCHMARK=OFF and -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_EXAMPLES=OFF: both default
# true and build programs that are not installed.
# -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_TCMALLOC=OFF: CMakeLists.txt:56-68 probes for
# libtcmalloc_minimal with pkg-config and enables itself if it finds one. It
# will not find one here, but that is a property of the image rather than of
# this recipe, so it is stated.
# -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF: the test suite needs gtest, and third_party/googletest is
# empty like the rest.
#
# The FORCE_SYSTEM flags are belt and braces. Each already takes the system path
# because its submodule directory is empty, so none of them changes today's
# behaviour -- they state the intent so that a future tarball that DOES bundle a
# copy cannot quietly switch this build onto it and ship a second, differently
# configured brotli or lcms2 inside libjxl.
#
# NOT SET, deliberately:
#
#   JPEGXL_ENABLE_TOOLS   left ON, its default. cjxl, djxl and jxlinfo are what
#                         make a broken decoder debuggable by hand, and BLFS
#                         installs them.
#   PROVISION_DEPENDENCIES  CMakeLists.txt:37-48 runs deps.sh under this, which
#                         DOWNLOADS every submodule from GitHub during configure
#                         and raises FATAL_ERROR if it cannot. It is undefined
#                         by default, so it does not run. Recorded because it is
#                         the one switch that would turn this from a build into
#                         a network fetch, and nothing else in the file warns
#                         about it.
#   BUILD_SHARED_LIBS     _scripts/build-cmake.sh passes ON already.
#   giflib                NOT A FLAG AND NOT NEEDED. BLFS lists giflib under
#                         "Required" for this package. The build file disagrees:
#                         lib/jxl_extras.cmake:38-45 is find_package(GIF 5.1)
#                         guarded by if(GIF_FOUND), so it is genuinely optional
#                         and costs only GIF input support in the tools. Read
#                         from the source rather than the dependency list, and
#                         the list was wrong in the expensive direction.
CMAKE_ARGS="-DBUILD_TESTING=OFF \
-DJPEGXL_ENABLE_PLUGINS=ON -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_PLUGIN_GIMP210=OFF \
-DJPEGXL_ENABLE_SKCMS=OFF -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_SJPEG=OFF \
-DJPEGXL_ENABLE_JPEGLI=OFF -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_JNI=OFF \
-DJPEGXL_ENABLE_OPENEXR=OFF -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_TCMALLOC=OFF \
-DJPEGXL_ENABLE_MANPAGES=OFF -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_DOXYGEN=OFF \
-DJPEGXL_ENABLE_BENCHMARK=OFF -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_EXAMPLES=OFF \
-DJPEGXL_FORCE_SYSTEM_HWY=ON -DJPEGXL_FORCE_SYSTEM_BROTLI=ON \
-DJPEGXL_FORCE_SYSTEM_LCMS2=ON"
